# Phishing — The Art of Digital Deception

90% of cyberattacks start with a phishing email.

## What is Phishing?
Social engineering attack where attacker pretends
to be a trusted source to steal credentials,
money, or sensitive information.

The attacker doesn't hack your system.
They hack YOUR MIND.

## How it Works
1. Attacker creates fake login page
2. Sends convincing email with malicious link
3. Victim clicks & enters credentials
4. Attacker captures everything
5. Victim never knows it happened

## Types of Phishing
Email Phishing    most common
Spear Phishing    targeted at specific person
Smishing          via SMS
Vishing           via phone call
Clone Phishing    copied real email
Whaling           targets CEOs & executives

## Fake Email Signs
→ Sender email looks slightly wrong
   real: support@paypal.com
   fake: support@paypa1.com
→ Creates urgency ("Act NOW!")
→ Generic greeting ("Dear Customer")
→ Suspicious attachments
→ Links don't match site name
→ Poor grammar & spelling

## Fake Website Signs
→ URL is slightly misspelled
→ No HTTPS padlock
→ Design looks slightly off
→ Asks for too much information

## How to Stay Safe
→ Always check the sender email carefully
→ Never click links in emails directly
→ Enable 2FA on all accounts
→ Use a password manager
→ Hover over links before clicking
→ When in doubt — don't click

## Real Example
Email: "Your account is suspended!
Click here to verify immediately."
Link:  https://paypa1.com/verify
Result: Password — STOLEN.

"Hackers don't break doors.
They knock — and you let them in."
